WITH input AS (
 SELECT * FROM jsonb_to_recordset($FORUM_EDITOR$[{"id":1,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA fictional stock shows a $0.15 bid/ask spread, shallow size and a stop $0.10 away. Decide ENTER, WATCH or NO TRADE and explain whether spread alone could consume the stop distance.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":2,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nFictional long entry $20.00, stop $19.50, highest subsequent observed price during the holding period $21.00 and lowest $19.80. Calculate 2.0R MFE and 0.4R MAE. Do not use bars after exit.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":3,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nAt 10:00 the observed HOD is $18.40 and LOD is $17.65. At 10:05 a new high prints. Explain how the reference changes and what evidence, beyond a touch, would support action.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":4,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nFor two hypothetical prints, 100 shares at $10 and 300 at $11, the illustrative volume-weighted average is $10.75. Explain why a single cross above VWAP does not validate a setup; real intraday VWAP uses the defined session's included trades.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":5,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nSeparate three observations: a displayed bid size, an executed trade price, and a quote cancellation. Which is a trade, which is only displayed interest, and what cannot be inferred about hidden orders? Identify the feed venue.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFeed scope: uploaded research sources STT-S-0232 (Nasdaq Basic) and STT-S-0233 (Nasdaq TotalView). Neither represents a consolidated all-venue historical order book. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":6,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nCompare two hypothetical journal records: a rule-following loss of 1R and an impulsive gain of 2R. Grade process adherence before outcome; propose a behavior change without claiming either record establishes expectancy.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":7,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA headline says an issuer is raising capital. Find the issuer's original filing, filing timestamp, security identity and offering terms before labeling the event bullish or bearish. Record what remains unknown.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFor issuer disclosure: SEC EDGAR, https://www.sec.gov/search-filings. Confirm original filing and event dates. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":8,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nAt a fictional 09:45 replay pause, record only bars completed by 09:45, the known catalyst and the candidate's invalidation. Advance one bar only after locking the decision; never import future candles into the initial answer.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource-side research: uploaded StocksToTrade-Browser-Research, October 22–24, 2026; examples without verified licensed OHLCV are not authenticated historical replay. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":9,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nDraft a helpful discussion using five fields: question, context, observed evidence, uncertainty, and what you want members to test. Do not ask others to coordinate purchases or post private records.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":10,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nWrite three separate fields for a fictional setup: reason (support and volume context), trigger (specific completed-bar behavior), invalidation (price/structure condition). Identify a no-trade case if the trigger never appears.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":11,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nThe quick tool map describes intended educational workflows, not a guarantee that each tool is deployed, enabled or included in your plan. Verify the current Account entitlement and actual tool screen; report any missing workflow rather than inventing a simulator fill or market-data source.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":12,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nStart on your member Dashboard, identify one current learning task, locate the authorized tool, complete its guided workflow and sign out. On return, distinguish a saved record from an unsaved form state; use private Support for account issues.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":13,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nChoose a Foundation chapter and search the Lab Registry by its canonical Lab ID. Verify whether the exercise is available to your account; record the learning objective and an unanswered question rather than assuming a registration is a completed lesson.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":14,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA chart after a future breakout would reveal the answer. At the simulated decision time, write the available time-stamped facts, decision, invalidation and missing evidence before advancing. Label a dataset synthetic until historical identity and licensing are verified.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource-side research: uploaded StocksToTrade-Browser-Research, October 22–24, 2026; examples without verified licensed OHLCV are not authenticated historical replay. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":15,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nUse fictional prices and label every fill as simulated. Account for spread, partial-fill possibility and a gap past a stop; a training tool cannot prove a real broker would have filled at your assumed price.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource-side research: uploaded StocksToTrade-Browser-Research, October 22–24, 2026; examples without verified licensed OHLCV are not authenticated historical replay. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":16,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nFor a fictional entry $10.00 and invalidation $9.75, express initial per-share risk as $0.25. Record the reason, decision timestamp, actual or fictional fill status, execution costs and rule adherence before measuring R outcomes.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":17,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nAsk Talia to explain VWAP in plain language, then request a guided fictional example and state your own decision before revealing feedback. Check the answer against the lesson; do not request a real-time buy or sell recommendation.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":18,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA scanner flags a price mover. List the candidate's timestamped volume, spread, news source, listing identity and liquidity risk. Explain why scanner inclusion initiates due diligence rather than approving an entry.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":19,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nFreeze the exact scanner filters, dataset timezone, session boundaries and test period before examining the results. Compare false positives and misses; do not select parameters after looking only at winning tickers.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource-side research: uploaded StocksToTrade-Browser-Research, October 22–24, 2026; examples without verified licensed OHLCV are not authenticated historical replay. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":20,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nFor a fictional watchlist, assign watch, conditional entry and reject. Add a trigger, invalidation, risk boundary and a cancellation time; an interesting ticker alone is not an executable trade plan.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":21,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nUse SEC EDGAR to find the issuer's primary filing. Distinguish the filing date from the event's effective date and from a news site's posting time; quote the relevant security terms in your own words.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFor issuer disclosure: SEC EDGAR, https://www.sec.gov/search-filings. Confirm original filing and event dates. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":22,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nWhen discussing float, distinguish shares outstanding, restricted shares, public float and potentially dilutive securities. A change in share count does not automatically tell you current freely tradeable supply.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFor issuer disclosure: SEC EDGAR, https://www.sec.gov/search-filings. Confirm original filing and event dates. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":23,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nMark only observed swing pivots. Compare a HH/HL sequence against a lower high and failed breakout, then state the first completed-bar evidence that changed your market-structure classification.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":24,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nUse a fictional daily trend for context, 5-minute chart for setup and 1-minute chart for execution observation. State why a 1-minute high is not proof of a daily trend reversal.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":25,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nFictional risk allowance $100, entry $20.00 and thesis invalidation $19.75 imply at most 400 shares before fees and slippage. Reduce the size further if spread, liquidity or actual risk budget requires; never size from buying power alone.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":26,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA hypothetical 500-share buy partially fills 200 at one price, then the remainder later at another. Compute the weighted-average fill and note that 'cancel requested' does not guarantee an unfilled order.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFor external order/market mechanics: SEC Investor.gov order types (updated August 2026), https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins-14. Data and broker availability vary. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":27,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA fictional $10.00 bid and $10.08 ask imply an $0.08 quoted spread. Explain the immediate round-trip cost before fees, whether visible size covers your quantity and why liquidity can vanish.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFeed scope: uploaded research sources STT-S-0232 (Nasdaq Basic) and STT-S-0233 (Nasdaq TotalView). Neither represents a consolidated all-venue historical order book. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":28,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nObserve a sequence of prints: trades at the ask, a changing best bid and size disappearing from one venue. Separate actual executions from quote changes; neither a single print nor one Level II book proves participant intent.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFeed scope: uploaded research sources STT-S-0232 (Nasdaq Basic) and STT-S-0233 (Nasdaq TotalView). Neither represents a consolidated all-venue historical order book. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":29,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nDefine setup, sample-selection rule, transaction costs, no-trade exclusions and out-of-sample period before tallying winners. Explain survivorship/look-ahead biases and why ten hand-picked winners do not establish repeatable expectancy.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource-side research: uploaded StocksToTrade-Browser-Research, October 22–24, 2026; examples without verified licensed OHLCV are not authenticated historical replay. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":30,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nCompare an issuer filing, an exchange notice and an anonymous social post about one fictional catalyst. Rank evidence by primary-source status, preserve timestamps and mark unverified claims explicitly.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFor issuer disclosure: SEC EDGAR, https://www.sec.gov/search-filings. Confirm original filing and event dates. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":31,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA hypothetical one-for-ten reverse split changes 1,000 pre-split shares into 100 post-split shares, ignoring fractional-share mechanics. Check effective date and adjusted/unadjusted charts before interpreting a percentage move.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFor issuer disclosure: SEC EDGAR, https://www.sec.gov/search-filings. Confirm original filing and event dates. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":32,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA fictional extended-hours bid is $8.00, ask $8.35 and displayed size is thin. Explain the impact of a $0.35 spread and which order types, sessions and hours your broker actually supports before assuming execution.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFor external order/market mechanics: SEC Investor.gov order types (updated August 2026), https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins-14. Data and broker availability vary. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":33,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA hypothetical volatility halt begins before your planned exit. The original stop may not execute at its intended price when trading reopens. Identify the exchange halt notice, reopening auction conditions and gap risk.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFor external order/market mechanics: SEC Investor.gov order types (updated August 2026), https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins-14. Data and broker availability vary. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":34,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA buy limit-on-open at $20.10 may not execute if the illustrative opening cross price is $20.15. Contrast this with market-on-open without assuming that any broker accepts either instruction at all times.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFor external order/market mechanics: SEC Investor.gov order types (updated August 2026), https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins-14. Data and broker availability vary. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":35,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nExplain the difference among market, limit, stop and stop-limit orders. A triggered stop-market order may execute away from its stop price; a stop-limit can remain unfilled. Verify the broker's specific instructions.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFor external order/market mechanics: SEC Investor.gov order types (updated August 2026), https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins-14. Data and broker availability vary. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":36,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nReview one fictional trade in this sequence: initial thesis, evidence and timestamp, execution versus plan, excursion within holding period, slippage, result and one process change. Do not reinterpret initial evidence using future bars.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":37,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA provider API key is a secret. Verify the provider's coverage, delayed-versus-live entitlement, pricing and redistribution terms; test connection with masked feedback. Never paste credentials into a public topic or screenshot.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":38,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nFor a forum question about a past candle, specify Lab ID, synthetic/historical status, time zone, completed bars, what you saw and where reasoning diverged. Report harassment privately, not by copying private messages.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":39,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nAfter a Foundations Book I lesson, explain one unfamiliar term in ordinary language, give a fictional illustration and identify a mistake a beginner could make. Use only the approved customer-edition chapter scope.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":40,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nAfter a Foundations Book II lesson, connect the observed candle or price structure to supporting evidence and invalidation. Label any historical example as unverified unless the registry supplies date, feed, adjustment and rights evidence.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource-side research: uploaded StocksToTrade-Browser-Research, October 22–24, 2026; examples without verified licensed OHLCV are not authenticated historical replay. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":41,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nFor Foundations Book III, distinguish an RCT exercise or risk calculation from an investment recommendation. Check the current approved WITH RCT customer edition rather than the archival WITHOUT RCT variant.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: Owner-approved project curriculum and product specifications. Operational availability and entitlements must be verified from the signed-in production service. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":42,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nDiscuss a day-trading setup through HOD/LOD, VWAP/EMA9/EMA20, volume, spread, risk and a NO TRADE alternative. A promised count of Lab registrations must not be represented as a count of production-accepted instructional sessions.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource-side research: uploaded StocksToTrade-Browser-Research, October 22–24, 2026; examples without verified licensed OHLCV are not authenticated historical replay. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":43,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nUse Time & Sales to distinguish bid-, ask- and midpoint-associated prints, then compare Level II book scope. Historical candles do not reconstruct an authentic historical order book or unobserved trade-by-trade feed.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFeed scope: uploaded research sources STT-S-0232 (Nasdaq Basic) and STT-S-0233 (Nasdaq TotalView). Neither represents a consolidated all-venue historical order book. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":76,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nNew founders: choose one approved learning area and post your question, not your payment history. Moderator access permits safety oversight, not Design Council voting or an entitlement to a founder number.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":77,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nDistinguish a nontransferable founding recognition number, a currently active subscription and a separately earned purchase discount. None gives ownership, dividends or authority to vote on company governance.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":78,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nFor any reported release, ask for the production URL, deployment revision, completed checks and an actual tested member workflow. A merged GitHub commit alone does not prove an eligible member can use the change.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":79,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA useful report identifies exact discussion or reply and a reason: spam, manipulation, harassment, privacy violation or misleading market claim. Do not repost the harmful content to attract attention.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":80,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nIntroduce yourself through learning goals, preferred chart timeframe and one topic you are practicing. A pseudonym is sufficient; never include legal name, home address, account numbers or health information.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":81,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nDescribe the exact misunderstanding, the example that corrected it and one new fictional case you can now explain independently. Do not treat a revealed assessment answer as evidence of mastery.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":82,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nAsk a focused question including the page name, expected action and observable error. Before posting, remove personal identity, payment data, auth tokens and screenshots of private account pages.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":83,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA learning milestone is an observed competency, such as recognizing a failed breakout with evidence at the pause. Share the method and transfer check, not a claimed trading return or another member's assessment answer.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":84,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nUse this non-sensitive defect template: affected URL or Lab ID; steps; expected result; actual result; timestamp/time zone; browser and viewport; accessibility effect; redacted evidence. Do not attach credentials.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":85,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nFor a fictional candle mismatch, record OHLC values, the formula you applied and the stage where Talia's explanation diverged. Include only visible fictional data, not protected grading answers or historical future bars.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":86,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nVerify keyboard-only navigation, visible focus, screen-reader labels, 200% zoom and reduced motion on the affected screen. Report exact controls and whether the issue blocks task completion.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":87,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nFor a checkout display defect, describe the route, visible non-sensitive error and browser context. Send invoice IDs, card details, disputes and identifying financial records only through authenticated private Support.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":88,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA proposal needs problem statement, affected role, current limitation, suggested behavior, measurable success and privacy/accessibility considerations. An approved forum idea is not permission to incur costs or promise delivery.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":89,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nCompare the same learning task on desktop, tablet and phone. State the precise navigation step that takes too long or is inaccessible, and propose a change that preserves keyboard and screen-reader access.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":90,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nRequest a different explanation, guided example or scaffolded retry for an identified Lab stage. Measure whether a beginner can articulate the underlying principle without hints, rather than only liking a presentation style.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":91,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nSpecify which of the approved 419 canonical Labs or Boot Camp competencies needs improvement, what evidence is missing and how a learner could demonstrate transfer. Do not announce an unbuilt feature as deployed.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":92,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nFor fictional O=10.00, H=10.80, L=9.80, C=10.60, range is 1.00, real body is 0.60 and body-to-range is 60%. State the zero-range special case and why candle geometry alone is not a forecast.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":93,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nCompare VWAP's session volume weighting with the EMA's exponentially weighted price series. A 9-period EMA on a 1-minute chart is not the same observation window as a 9-period EMA on 5-minute bars.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":94,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nMark completed higher-high/higher-low pivots in a fictional sequence, then flag the first confirmed lower high or failed reclaim. Separate what was visible at the decision time from what a later candle showed.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":95,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nAt a hypothetical 10.00 bid/10.10 ask, explain why the spread alters entry/exit costs. A large displayed ask may disappear or be executed; Time & Sales only reports prints from its defined feed.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nFeed scope: uploaded research sources STT-S-0232 (Nasdaq Basic) and STT-S-0233 (Nasdaq TotalView). Neither represents a consolidated all-venue historical order book. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":96,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nCompare renewal cadence rather than credit expiry: Founding 30-Day is recorded at $49.99 per 30 days and Founding 60-Day at $59.99 per 60 days, subject to the actual eligible Store offer. Database catalogue entries do not prove public launch or current checkout availability. Sparks issued under the approved V2 policy do not expire.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":97,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA percentage discount applies only to an eligible first-party separate purchase after authorization. Illustrate 10% versus 15% on a fictional $100 qualifying product ($90 versus $85 before tax), and verify Lifetime eligibility and stacking rules in the current official Store.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":99,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nDistinguish cancelling future renewal from deleting an account, refunding a payment or losing a permanently assigned founder number. Verify state changes in private Account/Billing; do not post personal invoices.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":100,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nStudy an official design ballot by comparing accessibility, performance, learning efficiency and privacy. Staff may inspect Council discussions for moderation but must not cast a founder vote without independently earned eligibility.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":101,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA desktop side panel that saves two clicks may still fail on a phone if it hides focus. Test tab order, escape behavior, zoom, text contrast and task completion before choosing the design.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":102,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nPropose one change to candle scaling, Talia's portrait size or correction feedback. Explain how it improves independent comprehension while preserving hidden assessment keys and instructor continuity.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":103,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nPrioritize two proposed improvements against severity, number of affected members, development effort and accessibility risk. Council preferences are input for Owner review, not binding corporate governance.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":104,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nCompare issue states with evidence: Submitted confirms receipt; Under Review needs triage; Accepted needs an approval record; Released requires deployment plus accepted verification. Avoid labelling a task complete from a green source test alone.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":105,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA useful bug record includes steps to reproduce, severity, affected member tier, expected and observed results and a regression test. Keep identity, billing, credentials and regulated data in the private support channel.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":106,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nWhen responding to a suggestion, record the rationale, owner, priority, dependencies, decision date, acceptance criteria and public-safe status. Explain a deferral without exposing private staff discussions.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."},{"id":107,"extra":"\n\n## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28\nA released improvement has an identifiable production commit/deployment, passing relevant checks and a successful member-facing workflow. A partial CI run, preview deployment or merged PR is not full release acceptance.\n\n## EVIDENCE AND DISCUSSION STANDARD\nSource: approved Founding 600 design plus production membership/Sparks rules. Consult the signed-in Store and Account for current eligibility, not this discussion for a quote. Discuss what was observable, what remains an inference, and what would invalidate the decision. Fictional calculations are teaching examples, not historical fills, performance claims or investment recommendations."}]$FORUM_EDITOR$::jsonb)
 AS x(id bigint,extra text)
), changed AS (
 UPDATE public.commons_topics t
 SET body=CASE WHEN t.id=96 THEN replace(t.body,'longer included-credit life','nonexpiring included Sparks') ELSE t.body END || i.extra,
     updated_at=now()
 FROM input i
 WHERE t.id=i.id AND t.id<=107 AND t.is_official=true AND t.status='published'
   AND position('## EDITORIAL FIELD EXERCISE — 2026-10-28' in t.body)=0
 RETURNING t.id,t.forum_code,octet_length(t.body) AS revised_bytes
), audit AS (
 INSERT INTO public.admin_audit_log(actor_user_id,action,target_type,target_id,details)
 SELECT (SELECT user_id FROM public.admin_user_roles WHERE role_code='OWNER'
          AND (expires_at IS NULL OR expires_at>now()) ORDER BY granted_at LIMIT 1),
  'forum.editorial.field_exercise_20261028','commons_topic',c.id::text,
  jsonb_build_object('revision','2026-10-28-field-exercise-v1','forum',c.forum_code,
                    'new_bytes',c.revised_bytes,'preserves_original',true)
 FROM changed c RETURNING id
)
SELECT (SELECT count(*) FROM input) AS expected,
       (SELECT count(*) FROM changed) AS updated,
       (SELECT count(*) FROM audit) AS audit_records,
       (SELECT array_agg(id ORDER BY id) FROM changed) AS updated_ids;
